<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gayatri Devi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/2009">2009</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gayatri Devi was an Indian princess and politician, born into the royal family of Cooch Behar, who became the third wife of Man Singh II, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a>. Admired for her beauty and style, she founded schools for girls in Jaipur and in 1962 won a seat in parliament for the Swatantra Party with a record majority. She was jailed during the Emergency of 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gayatri-devi.jpg" alt="Gayatri Devi" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vivienne · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharani_Gayatri_Devi_of_Jaipur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
